    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nI got\n```\n(mini.ai) No textobject \"if\" found covering region within 500 lines and `search_method = 'cover_or_next'`.   \n```\nwhen I try to `vif` or `vaf` when cursor located inside the function:\n```\nfn main() {\n    // This is a simple Rust program that prints \"Hello, World!\" to the console.\n    println!(\"Hello, World!\");\n}\n```\n\nWhen I uncomment `use_nvim_treesitter = true` in init.lua or use `nvim-treesitter.configs -> textobjects` - everything works as expected.\n\nI found https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1836, looks similar, but not the same and should be already fixed\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```sh\n$ nvim --version\nNVIM v0.12.0-dev-644+g487112d674\nBuild type: RelWithDebInfo\nLuaJIT 2.1.1748459687\nRun \"nvim -V1 -v\" for more info\n```\n\ninit.lua:\n```lua\n-- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nlocal clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim', mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\nrequire('mini.deps').setup()\n\nMiniDeps.add({\n  source = 'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter',\n  checkout = 'master',\n  hooks = { post_checkout = function() vim.cmd('TSUpdate') end },\n})\nMiniDeps.add({\n  source = 'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects',\n  checkout = 'master',\n})\n\nrequire('nvim-treesitter.configs').setup({\n  ensure_installed = { 'rust' },\n  auto_install = true,\n  highlight = { enable = true },\n  -- textobjects = {\n  --   select = {\n  --     enable = true,\n  --     keymaps = {\n  --       [\"af\"] = \"@function.outer\",\n  --       [\"if\"] = \"@function.inner\",\n  --     },\n  --   }\n  -- }\n})\n\n\nlocal treesitter = require('mini.ai').gen_spec.treesitter\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\n  n_lines = 500,\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    f = treesitter(\n      {\n        a = '@function.outer',\n        i = '@function.inner'\n      }\n      -- , { use_nvim_treesitter = true }\n    )\n  }\n})\n```\n\n\n`$ NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim main.rs`",
