        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis is because query file for the Rust language [uses custom `#make-range!` directive](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/89ebe73cd2836db80a22d9748999ace0241917a5/queries/rust/textobjects.scm#L15) for `@function.inner`, which is [not supported with `use_nvim_treesitter = false`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3f5d06a6f710966cb93baaadc4897eeb6d6210e5/doc/mini-ai.txt#L753-L757) (which is the new default).\n\nThe `af` textobject works with reproduction code, because it doesn't involve `#make-range!` directive.\n\nThe `use_nvim_treesitter = true` makes `if` textobject work because 'nvim-treesitter' itself (on `master` branch) implements that kind of directive support.\n\nThe way forward will be to focus on supporting the `main` branch of 'nvim-treesitter-textboejcts' (when it is made default), as it doesn't include custom directives. But it would still require #1850 to be merged, which I'll hope to get to soon.\n\nSo for the time being explicitly setting `use_nvim_treesitter = true` with `master` branch is the suggested approach. Or write custom query for `@function.inner` that doesn't use `#make-range!` directive.\n\nClosing as a documented limitation of the 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' queries on `master` branch.",
